.* DSPMSG and WRKMSG: a message queue's messages at the intermediate
.* assistance level (Display Messages, a reply field under each
.* inquiry that waits) and at the basic level (Work with Messages,
.* the inquiries that wait apart from the rest), and the Additional
.* Message Information panels shown for one message.
:PNLGRP.
:COPYR.(C) Quartz Systems 2026
:CLASS NAME=NAMECL BASETYPE='CHAR 10'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=SEVCL BASETYPE='CHAR 2'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=LINECL BASETYPE='CHAR 77'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=WLINECL BASETYPE='CHAR 72'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=TYPECL BASETYPE='CHAR 13'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=DATECL BASETYPE='CHAR 8'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=FLAGCL BASETYPE='CHAR 1'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=RPYCL BASETYPE='CHAR 60'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=LRPYCL BASETYPE='CHAR 61'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=OPTCL BASETYPE=ACTION.
:ECLASS.
:VAR NAME=SYSNM CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=MSGQ CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=MSGQLIB CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=PGM CLASS=NAMECL VALUE='*DSPMSG'.
:VAR NAME=PGMLIB CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=SEV CLASS=SEVCL VALUE='00'.
:VAR NAME=DLVRY CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=KSET CLASS=FLAGCL VALUE='0'.
:VAR NAME=LINE CLASS=LINECL.
:VAR NAME=RPY CLASS=LRPYCL.
:VAR NAME=RPYOK CLASS=FLAGCL.
:VAR NAME=OPT CLASS=OPTCL.
:VAR NAME=FIRST CLASS=FLAGCL.
:VAR NAME=WLINE CLASS=WLINECL.
:VAR NAME=WHEAD CLASS=WLINECL.
:VAR NAME=FROMUSR CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=MSGSEV CLASS=SEVCL.
:VAR NAME=MSGTYPE CLASS=TYPECL.
:VAR NAME=SNTDATE CLASS=DATECL.
:VAR NAME=SNTTIME CLASS=DATECL.
:VAR NAME=REPLY CLASS=RPYCL.
:LISTDEF NAME=MSGS VARS='LINE RPY RPYOK'.
:LISTDEF NAME=WMSGS VARS='OPT FIRST WLINE WHEAD'.
:LISTDEF NAME=INFO VARS='LINE'.
:COND NAME=SET0 EXPR='&KSET. EQ "0"'.
:COND NAME=SET1 EXPR='&KSET. EQ "1"'.
.* The key rows are laid out at fixed columns, as the display shows
.* them: one item carries each row's text, the others act unseen.
:KEYL NAME=MSGKEYS HELP=KEYSHLP.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION='RETURN 1'.
:KEYI KEY=F1 ACTION='RETURN 1'.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT COND=SET0.F3=Exit              F11=Remove a message                 F12=Cancel
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT COND=SET1.F10=Display all            F21=Select assistance level
:KEYI KEY=F5 ACTION='RETURN 5'.
:KEYI KEY=F10 ACTION='RETURN 10'.
:KEYI KEY=F11 ACTION='RETURN 11'.
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.
:KEYI KEY=F13 ACTION='RETURN 13' COND=SET0.F13=Remove all       F16=Remove all except unanswered     F24=More keys
:KEYI KEY=F13 ACTION='RETURN 13' COND=SET1.F22=Display list details   F24=More keys
:KEYI KEY=F16 ACTION='RETURN 16'.
:KEYI KEY=F17 ACTION=TOP.
:KEYI KEY=F18 ACTION=BOTTOM.
:KEYI KEY=F21 ACTION='RETURN 21'.
:KEYI KEY=F22 ACTION='RETURN 22'.
:KEYI KEY=F24 ACTION='RETURN 24'.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEUP ACTION=PAGEUP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEDOWN ACTION=PAGEDOWN.
:EKEYL.
:KEYL NAME=WRKKEYS HELP=KEYSHLP.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F1 ACTION=HELP COND=SET0.F1=Help   F3=Exit   F5=Refresh   F6=Display system operator messages
:KEYI KEY=F1 ACTION=HELP COND=SET1.F12=Cancel   F18=Bottom    F21=Select assistance level
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.
:KEYI KEY=F5 ACTION='RETURN 5'.
:KEYI KEY=F6 ACTION='RETURN 6'.
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.
:KEYI KEY=F16 ACTION='RETURN 16' COND=SET0.F16=Remove messages not needing a reply   F17=Top   F24=More keys
:KEYI KEY=F16 ACTION='RETURN 16' COND=SET1.F22=Display list details   F24=More keys
:KEYI KEY=F17 ACTION=TOP.
:KEYI KEY=F18 ACTION=BOTTOM.
:KEYI KEY=F21 ACTION='RETURN 21'.
:KEYI KEY=F22 ACTION='RETURN 22'.
:KEYI KEY=F24 ACTION='RETURN 24'.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEUP ACTION=PAGEUP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEDOWN ACTION=PAGEDOWN.
:EKEYL.
:KEYL NAME=OPRKEYS HELP=KEYSHLP.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F1 ACTION=HELP.F1=Help   F3=Exit      F5=Refresh   F6=Display your messages   F12=Cancel
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.
:KEYI KEY=F5 ACTION='RETURN 5'.
:KEYI KEY=F6 ACTION='RETURN 6'.
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.
:KEYI KEY=F17 ACTION=TOP.F17=Top   F18=Bottom   F22=Display list details
:KEYI KEY=F18 ACTION=BOTTOM.
:KEYI KEY=F21 ACTION='RETURN 21'.
:KEYI KEY=F22 ACTION='RETURN 22'.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEUP ACTION=PAGEUP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEDOWN ACTION=PAGEDOWN.
:EKEYL.
:KEYL NAME=INFOKEYS HELP=KEYSHLP.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F1 ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F6 ACTION=PRINT.F6=Print
:KEYI KEY=F9 ACTION='RETURN 9'.F9=Display message details
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:KEYI KEY=F21 ACTION='RETURN 21'.F21=Select assistance level
:KEYI KEY=PAGEUP ACTION=PAGEUP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEDOWN ACTION=PAGEDOWN.
:EKEYL.
:PANEL NAME=DSPMSG KEYL=MSGKEYS HELP=DSPMSGH ENTER='RETURN 0' TOPSEP=NONE BOTSEP=NONE.Display Messages
:DATA DEPTH=1.
:DATACOL WIDTH=54.
:DATAC.
:DATACOL WIDTH=24.
:DATAC.System:   &SYSNM.
:EDATA.
:DATA DEPTH=4.
:DATACOL WIDTH=44.
:DATAC.Queue . . . . . :   &MSGQ.
:DATAGRP GRPSEP=NONE.
:DATAC.Library . . . :     &MSGQLIB.
:EDATAGRP.
:DATAC.Severity  . . . :   &SEV.
:DATACOL WIDTH=34.
:DATAC.Program . . . . :   &PGM.
:DATAGRP GRPSEP=NONE.
:DATAC.Library . . . :     &PGMLIB.
:EDATAGRP.
:DATAC.Delivery  . . . :   &DLVRY.
:EDATA.
:TOPINST.Type reply (if required), press Enter.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=MSGS SCROLL=YES.
:LISTCOL VAR=LINE USAGE=OUTPUT.
:LISTCOL VAR=RPY USAGE=INOUT ATCOL=20 IFVAR=RPYOK.
:ELIST.
:EPANEL.
:PANEL NAME=WRKMSG KEYL=WRKKEYS HELP=WRKMSGH ENTER='RETURN 0' TOPSEP=SYSNAM BOTSEP=NONE.Work with Messages
:DATA DEPTH=2.
:DATACOL WIDTH=78.
:DATAC.Messages for:   &MSGQ.
:EDATA.
:TOPINST.Type options below, then press Enter.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=WMSGS SCROLL=YES ACTLEN=1 HELP=WRKOPTH.
:LISTACT OPTION=4 ENTER='RETURN 4' HELP=WRKOPTH.4=Remove
:LISTACT OPTION=5 ENTER='RETURN 5' HELP=WRKOPTH.5=Display details and reply
:LISTCOL VAR=OPT USAGE=INPUT IFVAR=FIRST.Opt
:LISTCOL VAR=WLINE USAGE=OUTPUT ATCOL=8.Message
:LISTCOL VAR=WHEAD USAGE=OUTPUT ATCOL=8 HILITE.
:ELIST.
:EPANEL.
:PANEL NAME=WRKOPR KEYL=OPRKEYS HELP=WRKMSGH ENTER='RETURN 0' TOPSEP=SYSNAM BOTSEP=NONE.Work with Messages
:DATA DEPTH=2.
:DATACOL WIDTH=78.
:DATAC.Messages for:   &MSGQ.
:EDATA.
:TOPINST.Type options below, then press Enter.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=WMSGS SCROLL=YES ACTLEN=1 HELP=WRKOPTH.
:LISTACT OPTION=5 ENTER='RETURN 5' HELP=WRKOPTH.5=Display details and reply
:LISTCOL VAR=OPT USAGE=INPUT IFVAR=FIRST.Opt
:LISTCOL VAR=WLINE USAGE=OUTPUT ATCOL=8.Message
:LISTCOL VAR=WHEAD USAGE=OUTPUT ATCOL=8 HILITE.
:ELIST.
:EPANEL.
:PANEL NAME=ADDMSGI KEYL=INFOKEYS HELP=ADDMSGH ENTER='RETURN 0' TOPSEP=SPACE.Additional Message Information
:DATA DEPTH=4.
:DATACOL WIDTH=41.
:DATAI VAR=FROMUSR USAGE=OUTPUT.From
:DATAI VAR=MSGTYPE USAGE=OUTPUT.Message type
:DATAI VAR=SNTDATE USAGE=OUTPUT.Date sent
:DATACOL WIDTH=37.
:DATAC.Severity . . . . . . . :   &MSGSEV.
:DATAC.
:DATAC.Time sent  . . . . . . :   &SNTTIME.
:EDATA.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=INFO SCROLL=YES.
:LISTCOL VAR=LINE USAGE=OUTPUT.
:ELIST.
:BOTINST.Press Enter to continue.
:EPANEL.
:PANEL NAME=ADDMSGR KEYL=INFOKEYS HELP=ADDMSGH ENTER='RETURN 0' TOPSEP=SPACE.Additional Message Information
:DATA DEPTH=4.
:DATACOL WIDTH=41.
:DATAI VAR=FROMUSR USAGE=OUTPUT.From
:DATAI VAR=MSGTYPE USAGE=OUTPUT.Message type
:DATAI VAR=SNTDATE USAGE=OUTPUT.Date sent
:DATACOL WIDTH=37.
:DATAC.Severity . . . . . . . :   &MSGSEV.
:DATAC.
:DATAC.Time sent  . . . . . . :   &SNTTIME.
:EDATA.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=INFO SCROLL=YES.
:LISTCOL VAR=LINE USAGE=OUTPUT.
:ELIST.
:TOPINST.Type reply below, then press Enter.
:DATA DEPTH=1.
:DATACOL WIDTH=14.
:DATACOL WIDTH=78.
:DATAI VAR=REPLY USAGE=INPUT CSRLOC.Reply
:EDATA.
:EPANEL.
:PANEL NAME=ADDMSGA KEYL=INFOKEYS HELP=ADDMSGH ENTER='RETURN 0' TOPSEP=SPACE.Additional Message Information
:DATA DEPTH=4.
:DATACOL WIDTH=41.
:DATAI VAR=FROMUSR USAGE=OUTPUT.From
:DATAI VAR=MSGTYPE USAGE=OUTPUT.Message type
:DATAI VAR=SNTDATE USAGE=OUTPUT.Date sent
:DATACOL WIDTH=37.
:DATAC.Severity . . . . . . . :   &MSGSEV.
:DATAC.
:DATAC.Time sent  . . . . . . :   &SNTTIME.
:EDATA.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=INFO SCROLL=YES.
:LISTCOL VAR=LINE USAGE=OUTPUT.
:ELIST.
:DATA DEPTH=1.
:DATACOL WIDTH=14.
:DATACOL WIDTH=78.
:DATAI VAR=REPLY USAGE=OUTPUT.Reply
:EDATA.
:BOTINST.Press Enter to continue.
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=DSPMSGH.Display Messages - Help
:P.The messages on a message queue, oldest first. An inquiry that
waits has a reply field under it: type the reply there and press
Enter. F1 on a message shows the whole of it.
:P.F11 removes the message under the cursor, F13 every message, F16
every message but the inquiries that still wait for a reply. F21
switches to the basic assistance level.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WRKMSGH.Work with Messages - Help
:P.The messages on a message queue, newest first: the inquiries that
wait for a reply, then the rest. Type 5 by one to see all of it and
answer it, 4 to remove it.
:P.F6 shows the system operator's messages, F16 removes every message
that does not need a reply, F21 switches to the intermediate
assistance level.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WRKOPTH.Options - Help
:P.Type an option by a message and press Enter.
:P.4 removes the message from its queue.
:P.5 shows the message whole, with what its description says, and
takes the reply when it is an inquiry that waits for one.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=ADDMSGH.Additional Message Information - Help
:P.The whole message: who sent it and when, its text and what the
message description says about its cause and what to do. F9 adds the
message identifier, its message file and the sending program.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=KEYSHLP.Function keys - Help
:P.F3 leaves the display, F12 goes back one display, F5 shows the
queue again as it is now.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
